  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is Cosmopolitan Church of Prayer?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Cosmopolitan Church of Prayer is a South Side Chicago congregation founded on April 29, 1959, by gospel singer and pastor Dr. Charles G. Hayes, beginning in the basement of a home at 634 Woodland Park. Gospel historian Robert M. Marovich counts it among the first Chicago churches to adopt the new Detroit gospel choral style. The congregation grew through a Cottage Grove Avenue storefront and, from 1961, a converted post office on South Langley Avenue, before settling at 842 East 65th Street in Woodlawn, the corner of 65th and Maryland the church calls \"Love Corner.\" Its choir, the Warriors, be"
   }
  },
  {
