    "text": "Chicago Baptist congregation; Mahalia Jackson's first Chicago church home after her 1927 arrival, and the base of her early choir work and the Johnson Brothers/Johnson Gospel Singers. Within months of arriving, Jackson was the lead vocalist of the 50-member choir and joined the pastor's sons (Prince, Wilbur, and Robert Johnson) and Louise Lemon in the Johnson Singers \u2014 described as Chicago's first Black gospel group. The Johnson Brothers were the first organized group to play the Chicago church circuit, staging self-written musical dramas at the church with Jackson in the lead role before spli"
   }
