   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is Mt. Zion Baptist Church?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Mt. Zion Baptist Church was a Washington Park, Chicago congregation pastored from 1968 to 1976 by the Rev. T. L. Barrett \u2014 the pastorate in which Barrett formed his Youth for Christ Choir and began the recording career collected decades later in the box set I Shall Wear a Crown. Barrett, whose pulpit career began in 1966, took the Mt. Zion pulpit in 1968; there he built a youth-focused ministry whose roughly forty-voice teenage choir recorded Like a Ship (Without a Sail) in 1971. In 1976, after a theological disagreement with the church's elders, Barrett left to found the Life Center Church of"
   }
  },
