   "name": "What is New Life Covenant Church Southeast?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "New Life Covenant Church Southeast is a nondenominational, multicultural congregation on Chicago's South Side founded and led by Pastor John F. Hannah. Church accounts describe a start on January 27, 2010, with about sixty people at a Wednesday-night Bible study. The congregation became known for an intense prayer culture \u2014 4 AM prayer gatherings, twelve-hour prayer events, and the annual Prayer on the 9 march that lines 79th Street \u2014 and worshiped at a site it calls The Tabernacle, at 78th and Dobson. In September 2021 it opened The Temple, a 100,000-square-foot, 4,000-seat worship and perfor"
   }
