   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is Shrine of Christ the King?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Roman Catholic shrine at 6401 S. Woodlawn Ave., Woodlawn, now administered by the Institute of Christ the King Sovereign Priest. Founded as St. Clara parish (1894); Renaissance Revival church by Henry J. Schlacks finished 1928; renamed St. Clara\u2013St. Cyril (1969) and St. Gelasius (1990); closed 2002; designated a Chicago Landmark January 14, 2004; damaged by fires in 1976 and 2015. Neighborhood: Woodlawn."
   }
  },
  {
