  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is Kennedy-King College theaters?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Performing-arts venue at Kennedy-King College, 740 W. 63rd St., Englewood, Chicago: the U Building's state-of-the-art 292-seat mainstage and black box theaters. Collaboraction Theatre Company staged its 2019\u201320 mainstage season ('We Are Each Other's Business') there \u2014 including the fourth annual Peacebook Festival and the 'Red Island' world premiere \u2014 as year three of its five-year One City plan. The U Building also houses the Center of Equity for Creative Arts (CECA) and WKKC-FM 89.3. Neighborhood: Englewood. Years active: 2019\u2013present. Status recorded October 2026: Operating."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
