    "text": "Warner Bros. neighborhood theater at 715 W. 63rd St, Englewood. Opened September 4, 1920, with 2,433 seats and a Moller 3-manual 22-rank organ; built for Cooney Brothers National Theaters Corp. Often said to be where Bob Hope got his first start. Torn down. Neighborhood: Englewood. Years active: 1920\u2013?. Status recorded October 2026: Demolished."
