   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The Harold Washington Library Center is the main branch of the Chicago Public Library. It is home to YOUmedia, the library's teen digital-learning program, which opened in 2009; Chicago rapper Noname spent time as a teen in the YOUMedia project at the Harold Washington Library. The building houses CPL's Special Collections Division, cited in a finding aid as the holder of the Kuumba collection; a Smithsonian Archives of American Art survey also places the George Cleveland Hall Branch Archives there \u2014 28 linear feet of records dating from 1932 to the 1970s, including remnants of the Special Neg"
   }
