   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Nightclub and dance hall at 459 East 31st Street (South Cottage Grove), the largest dance hall on Chicago's South Side until the Savoy Ballroom opened in 1927. Reinvented in 1918 by Black entrepreneurs Virgil Williams and William Bottoms; renamed Lincoln Gardens in 1921. Resident home of King Oliver's Creole Jazz Band (1922\u20131924), where Louis Armstrong came north to play second cornet. Closed June 1927 after a bombing. Years active: 1922\u20131928."
   }
  },
