    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The White City Ballroom was the ballroom of the White City Amusement Park at 63rd Street and South Park Avenue (now Dr. Martin Luther King Jr. Drive), on the Woodlawn / Greater Grand Crossing edge of the South Side. The park opened on May 26, 1905 (one Illinois history source gives May 27 \u2014 a minor contradiction the corpus notes), spread over fourteen acres, and rivaled Coney Island; its ballroom was built for 1,000 dancers, alongside the College Inn restaurant seating 2,500. The graph record describes it as a big-band ballroom within White City, and the University of Chicago's jazz guide \u2014 th"
   }
